camilladsp: policy surface for the placeholder-free slot model

- GetPolicy websocket command: the active manifest IS the enforced
  policy; serve it (subchains + mixers) so web UIs render the editable
  surface from WS data alone. Unprotected: {"protected": false}.
- Manifest validation: editable sub chains are attributed by the step
  description (genconf renders the uci section id there) instead of the
  user_slot_* placeholder anchors - every pipeline step is a real step
  defined 1:1 in uci, its names carry base filter(s) + web UI additions.
- Policy-level free gaps become slot indexes (locked anchors preceding
  the step, computed by genconf) instead of anchor names.

Regenerated against pristine upstream + the committed 0001..0004 (the
previous regeneration used a contaminated baseline and failed fresh
extracts with 4/7 rejected hunks).

Signed-off-by: virgilio firmware
